# MCP Server: {{ service_name }}

Auto-generated MCP server wrapping the **{{ service_name }}** MFS microservice.

## Quick Start

### 1. Install dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 2. Start the MFS service
```bash
# From the MFS root:
docker compose up -d --build
```

### 3. Run the MCP server
```bash
# stdio transport (for Claude Desktop, Codex, etc.)
python server.py

# SSE transport (for web-based MCP clients)
python server.py --transport sse --port {{ mcp_port }}
```

### 4. Connect from Claude Desktop
Add to your Claude Desktop MCP config (`claude_desktop_config.json`):
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{ feature_slug }}": {
      "command": "python",
      "args": ["{{ output_path }}/server.py"]
    }
  }
}
```

### 5. Use with EasyMCP (complementary path)
```bash
easymcp create {{ feature_slug }} \
  --openapi {{ output_path }}/openapi.json \
  --port {{ mcp_port }}

easymcp start {{ feature_slug }}
easymcp agent install codex {{ feature_slug }}
```

